ue indicates messages are retained as Application Logs also along with Production History.\r\n- A List of messages to be migrated. The MessageIdOwnerList property takes the input in the form of a combination of message Id and Owner.","FullInfo":"Migrates Application Log Messages to Production History Records. During migration, the command deletes or retains the Application Log messages depending on the input property configuration.\r\nThe command takes the following input:\r\n- A True / False value for the DeleteMigratedApplicationLogMessages input property. A True value indicates deleting of messages as Apllication Logs after migration to Production History. A False value indicates messages are retained as Application Logs also along with Production History.\r\n- A List of messages to be migrated. The MessageIdOwnerList property takes the input in the form of a combination of message Id and Owner.","InfoMap":{"$id":"1361","FullIdObj":{"$id":"1362","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"Migrates Application Log Messages to Production History Records. During migration, the command deletes or retains the Application Log messages depending on the input property configuration.\r\nThe command takes the following input:\r\n- A True / False value for the DeleteMigratedApplicationLogMessages input property. A True value indicates deleting of messages as Apllication Logs after migration to Production History. A False value indicates messages are retained as Application Logs also along with Production History.\r\n- A List of messages to be migrated. The MessageIdOwnerList property takes the input in the form of a combination of message Id and Owner.","FullInfo":"Migrates Application Log Messages to Production History Records. During migration, the command deletes or retains the Application Log messages depending on the input property configuration.\r\nThe command takes the following input:\r\n- A True / False value for the DeleteMigratedApplicationLogMessages input property. A True value indicates deleting of messages as Apllication Logs after migration to Production History. A False value indicates messages are retained as Application Logs also along with Production History.\r\n- A List of messages to be migrated. The MessageIdOwnerList property takes the input in the form of a combination of message Id and Owner.","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"1362"},"Children":[],"Name":"Documentation","SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"Migrates Application Log Messages to Production History Records. During migration, the command deletes or retains the Application Log messages depending on the input property configuration.\r\nThe command takes the following input:\r\n- A True / False value for the DeleteMigratedApplicationLogMessages input property. A True value indicates deleting of messages as Apllication Logs after migration to Production History. A False value indicates messages are retained as Application Logs also along with Production History.\r\n- A List of messages to be migrated. The MessageIdOwnerList property takes the input in the form of a combination of message Id and Owner.","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"Migrates Application Log Messages to Production History Records. During migration, the command deletes or retains the Application Log messages depending on the input property configuration.\r\nThe command takes the following input:\r\n- A True / False value for the DeleteMigratedApplicationLogMessages input property. A True value indicates deleting of messages as Apllication Logs after migration to Production History. A False value indicates messages are retained as Application Logs also along with Production History.\r\n- A List of messages to be migrated. The MessageIdOwnerList property takes the input in the form of a combination of message Id and Owner."},"SystemAnnotations":[{"$id":"1363","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"Protected","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"1118"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"Protected","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"Protected"}],"CustomAnnotations":[{"$id":"1364","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"@Guid(53319f42-1743-40ab-94d8-354872f5c2fe)","FullInfo":"@Guid(53319f42-1743-40ab-94d8-354872f5c2fe)","InfoMap":{"$id":"1365","FullIdObj":{"$id":"1366","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"@Guid(53319f42-1743-40ab-94d8-354872f5c2fe)","FullInfo":"@Guid(53319f42-1743-40ab-94d8-354872f5c2fe)","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"1366"},"Children":[],"Name":"CustomAnnotation","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"1118"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"@Guid(53319f42-1743-40ab-94d8-354872f5c2fe)","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"@Guid(53319f42-1743-40ab-94d8-354872f5c2fe)"}],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"MigrateApplicationLogMessageToProductionHistoryRecord","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"MigrateApplicationLogMessageToProductionHistoryRecord"},{"$id":"1367","$type":"DslCommandInputDeclarationTree","Children":[{"$id":"1368","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"WITH","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"1118"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"WITH","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"WITH"},{"$id":"1369","$type":"DslCommandPropertyCollectionTree","Name":"InputProperties","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"1118"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"ChildrenList":[{"$id":"1370","$type":"DslCommandPropertyTree","Children":[{"$id":"1371","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"DeleteMigratedApplicationLogMessages","FullInfo":"Siemens.OpcenterEX.FN.OperationalData.ProductionHistory_OP.OPModel.Commands.MigrateApplicationLogMessageToProductionHistoryRecord.DeleteMigratedApplicationLogMessages","InfoMap":{"$id":"1372","FullIdObj":{"$id":"1373","$type":"IdentificableFakeProperty","Name":"DeleteMigratedApplicatio